  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 123,
      "char_start": 670,
      "char_end": 1218,
      "text": "There were French\nand Swedish sailors in their red woollen shirts, Norwegians and Danes in\nblue, with white canvas trousers, Yankees and English all in blue; and\nas they swung the gracefully dressed Dutch girls with their small white\ncaps and little capes, and petticoats fastened up to do justice to the\nneat shoes and white stockings below, vying with each other who should\ndance the best and longest, the foundation of many a friendship or\nenmity was laid, to be prosecuted later on in the evening over a bottle\nof brandy or in a stand-up fight"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 121,
      "char_start": 287,
      "char_end": 700,
      "text": "They come on\nshore bursting with a full masculine longing for the society of the\nother sex, with a year's stored-up feeling to let out; and there is a\npositive intoxication to them in the mere dance--in the mere holding at\nNieuwediep Anniken or Bibecke, or at Portsmouth Mary Ann, by the waist;\nand Mary Ann and Bibecke perfectly understand this, and for the moment\nfeel themselves persons of no small importance"
    }
  ],
